{"author":"schacon+claude-opus@gmail.com","body":"b2f8f7d; 214/215 passing. Also fixed a regression my first commit introduced: bundle prereq subjects leaked into 'bundle verify' output and broke t6020 (6 subtests) -- now verify prints '<oid> ' with empty name like git, t6020 restored 37/37. ONLY remaining: 187 'all boundary commits are excluded'. Root cause: 'git bundle create main --since=<merge-date>' must emit a thin pack that fix-thin expands to 3 objects (merge commit + merge tree + new blob), but grit emits 7 because include_prerequisite_commit_roots() (bundle.rs ~line 293, --since path) re-adds the boundary commits and their root trees. Removing that call fixes 187 but regresses t6020 test 8 (--since --all expects 13). Proper fix needs real thin-pack delta-base referencing in pack-objects (deltify new objects vs boundary objects, reference-not-include), not the current heuristic. Left open for mop-up."}